    <h2 id="who-we-are">1. WHO WE ARE</h2>
    <p><strong>Controller:</strong> Cogniosynthesis Portal Ltd, company number 16225073, registered office 15 Neptune Court, Vanguard Way, Cardiff CF24 5PJ. We are registered in England and Wales and trade as CognioNews, CognioEngine and FestivalFocus.</p>
    <p>This notice covers <strong>cogniosynthesisportal.uk</strong> and its subdomains, and the services we provide through them. Where a specific product has its own additional notice, that notice applies alongside this one.</p>
    <p>We are registered with the Information Commission, the UK data protection regulator, under registration number ZC269688.</p>
    <p>We have not appointed a data protection officer, because the law does not require us to. Kenny Lewis, Director, is responsible for data protection. You can contact us about anything in this notice at <a href="mailto:privacy@cogniosynthesisportal.uk">privacy@cogniosynthesisportal.uk</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="what-data-we-collect">2. WHAT PERSONAL DATA WE COLLECT</h2>
    <p>We collect only what we need to run the service and to deal with you as a customer, reader or business contact.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Contact and account data:</strong> name, email address, and where relevant your organisation, role and telephone number, when you subscribe, register, submit a story or contact us.</li>
      <li><strong>Subscription and payment data:</strong> the plan you hold, its status, billing period and renewal date, and payment references from Stripe. Stripe collects and holds your card details. We do not receive or store your card number, expiry date or security code.</li>
      <li><strong>Content you give us:</strong> story submissions, comments, survey responses, emails and other messages you send us, including any files you attach.</li>
      <li><strong>Usage and device data:</strong> the pages you view on this site, the page you arrived from, approximate location (city level), device type, browser and operating system, and your IP address in our server logs.</li>
      <li><strong>Correspondence and support records:</strong> the history of your enquiries and our replies.</li>
      <li><strong>Business prospect data:</strong> see the supplementary section on B2B prospect data below.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>If you subscribe to CognioNews Premium, you need to give us your email address to subscribe and sign in. Without it we cannot provide Premium. The <a href="https://cognionews.com/privacy.html#premium">CognioNews privacy notice</a> describes the Premium data in full.</p>
    <p>We do <strong>not</strong> knowingly collect special category data (for example health, ethnicity, religion, political opinions, biometric or genetic data), and we do not buy personal data from data brokers.</p>

    <h2 id="audits">3. AUDITS</h2>
    <p>We carry out Epistemic Audits and AI Health Checks at your premises on our own machine, which is not connected to the internet or to your network. Your documents are loaded from your own storage, are never sent to us, and are not kept: at the end of the visit the machine is wiped clean in front of you and you receive a signed visit record of what was loaded, what was produced and when it was wiped clean. We keep one copy of the signed visit record: the date, the number of files, their digital fingerprints, the start and finish times, and the name of the person from your team who was present. It holds no file names and no document content. We keep it for six years as our business record. We do not use your documents to train any system. The written finding belongs to you.</p>

    <h2 id="how-we-use-data">4. HOW WE USE YOUR PERSONAL DATA</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To provide the service: publishing content, delivering the pages you request, and managing your access and preferences.</li>
      <li>To create and administer your subscription or account, and to take and manage payment.</li>
      <li>To send you the newsletters, digests and service messages you have asked for, and to handle unsubscribes.</li>
      <li>To answer your enquiries, deal with complaints and provide support.</li>
      <li>To keep our own records, including accounting, tax and VAT records required by law.</li>
      <li>To keep the service secure and available: detecting abuses, fraud, scraping, attacks and technical faults.</li>
      <li>To introduce our services to named people at organisations, under the B2B section below.</li>
      <li>To establish, exercise or defend legal claims.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not use your personal data for automated decision-making that produces legal or similarly significant effects about you, and we do not sell your personal data. Our AI analysis is applied to published news content and, during an on-site audit, to the documents a client chooses to load on our offline machine (see section 3), not to profiles of individual readers.</p>

    <h2 id="lawful-bases">5. OUR LAWFUL BASES</h2>
    <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse;">
      <tr><th style="border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 8px; text-align: left;">Purpose</th><th style="border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 8px; text-align: left;">Lawful basis (UK GDPR)</th></tr>
      <tr><td style="border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 8px;">Providing the service you have asked for, including a paid subscription such as CognioNews Premium, and administering your subscription or account</td><td style="border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 8px;">Performance of a contract — Article 6(1)(b)</td></tr>
      <tr><td style="border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 8px;">Taking payment and managing billing, refunds and cancellations</td><td style="border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 8px;">Performance of a contract — Article 6(1)(b)</td></tr>
