      <tr><td style="border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 8px;">Billing records, accounting, tax and other statutory records</td><td style="border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 8px;">Legal obligation — Article 6(1)(c)</td></tr>
      <tr><td style="border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 8px;">Establishing, exercising or defending legal claims</td><td style="border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 8px;">Legitimate interests — Article 6(1)(f), or legal obligation where a claim is compulsory</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h2 id="who-we-share-with">6. WHO WE SHARE IT WITH</h2>
    <p>We do not sell personal data. We share it only where we need to in order to run the service, and only with organisations that are bound to protect it.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Payment processing:</strong> Stripe Payments UK Ltd and the Stripe group. Stripe processes card data as an independent controller for payment processing and fraud prevention. We receive limited transaction data back from Stripe to reconcile your subscription.</li>
      <li><strong>Hosting and infrastructure:</strong> our hosting provider, with servers in the United Kingdom. It hosts our websites, server logs and service data.</li>
      <li><strong>Email delivery:</strong> our email provider (UK), which sends our newsletters and service emails such as receipts and sign-in links.</li>
      <li><strong>Professional advisers:</strong> our accountants, auditors and lawyers, where necessary and under duties of confidence.</li>
      <li><strong>Authorities and third parties:</strong> where we are required by law, by a court order, or where necessary to establish, exercise or defend legal claims, or to protect someone's vital interests.</li>
      <li><strong>Business transfers:</strong> if we sell or transfer all or part of the business, relevant data may be transferred to the buyer under equivalent protections.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not use advertising networks or social media tracking pixels on this site, and we do not share personal data for others' marketing.</p>

    <h2 id="international-transfers">7. INTERNATIONAL TRANSFERS</h2>
    <p>Our hosting provider's servers are in the United Kingdom, and our email provider is in the United Kingdom. Some of our processors are based in, or may access data from, the United States:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Stripe, LLC</strong> — covered by the UK–US Data Bridge (the UK Extension to the EU–US Data Privacy Framework). If the Data Bridge cannot be used, Stripe's Data Transfers Addendum applies the UK International Data Transfer Addendum instead.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Where we transfer personal data outside the UK, we rely on UK adequacy regulations, including the UK–US Data Bridge. If those regulations stop applying to a recipient, we will only continue the transfer under another lawful safeguard, such as the UK International Data Transfer Addendum, after checking that the transfer meets the legal test for that safeguard. You can ask us for details of the safeguards used for a particular transfer.</p>

