    <h2 id="your-rights">9. YOUR RIGHTS</h2>
    <p>Under UK data protection law, you have the following rights:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Right of access:</strong> You can ask for a copy of the personal data we hold about you.</li>
      <li><strong>Right to rectification:</strong> You can ask us to correct inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
      <li><strong>Right to erasure:</strong> You can ask us to delete your personal data in certain circumstances.</li>
      <li><strong>Right to restrict processing:</strong> You can ask us to limit how we use your data in certain circumstances.</li>
      <li><strong>Right to data portability:</strong> You can ask for your data in a structured, machine-readable format and transfer it to another service.</li>
      <li><strong>Right to object:</strong> You can object to our use of your personal data for direct marketing, and in some other circumstances.</li>
      <li><strong>Right not to be subject to automated decision-making:</strong> You have the right not to be subject to a decision based solely on automated processing, including profiling, which produces legal effects or similarly significantly affects you. We do not use such processing about individuals. Our AI analysis is applied to published news content and, during an on-site audit, to the documents a client chooses to load on our offline machine.</li>
      <li><strong>Right to complain:</strong> You have the right to complain to us or to the Information Commission.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="cookies-and-choices">10. COOKIES AND CHOICES</h2>
    <p>This site sets no cookies and runs no analytics. You can browse without giving us any personal data except what you choose to put in a form or an email.</p>

    <h2 id="b2b-prospect-data">11. B2B PROSPECT DATA</h2>
    <p>We sometimes introduce our services to named people at organisations we think could benefit from them. We do this under the legitimate interests lawful basis.</p>
    <p><strong>What we use:</strong> Name, work email address, job title, and organisation name — collected from public sources (company websites, LinkedIn, conference lists) or given to us at an event. We do not use personal email addresses (for example @gmail.com) for B2B outreach.</p>
    <p><strong>What we send:</strong> One initial introduction email, and, if you engage, further emails about our services. You can ask us to stop at any time by emailing <a href="mailto:privacy@cogniosynthesisportal.uk">privacy@cogniosynthesisportal.uk</a> or using the unsubscribe link in any email.</p>
    <p><strong>How long we keep it:</strong> We keep your contact details for 12 months from our last contact with you. If you ask us to stop contacting you, we keep a minimal suppression record so we do not email you again.</p>
    <p><strong>Your rights:</strong> You have the right to object to this use of your data. If you do, we will stop contacting you and will delete your details except for a minimal suppression record.</p>

    <h2 id="data-security">12. DATA SECURITY</h2>
    <p>We take appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect your personal data against unauthorised access, loss, destruction or damage. These include encryption in transit and at rest, access controls, regular security updates, and staff training.</p>

    <h2 id="data-breaches">13. DATA BREACHES</h2>
    <p>If a personal data breach is likely to put your rights and freedoms at risk, we will report it to the Information Commission, where feasible within 72 hours of becoming aware of it. If it is likely to put you at high risk, we will tell you without undue delay. We keep a record of every breach and what we did about it.</p>

    <h2 id="complaints">14. COMPLAINTS</h2>
    <p>If you are unhappy with how we have used your personal data, you have the right to complain to us. Email <a href="mailto:privacy@cogniosynthesisportal.uk">privacy@cogniosynthesisportal.uk</a> or write to Cogniosynthesis Portal Ltd, 15 Neptune Court, Vanguard Way, Cardiff CF24 5PJ. We will acknowledge your complaint within 30 days, look into it, keep you updated and tell you the outcome without undue delay.</p>
    <p>You also have the right to complain to the Information Commission, the UK data protection regulator. It replaced the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) on 30 September 2026.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Website: <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint</a></li>
      <li>Helpline: 0303 123 1113</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="changes">15. CHANGES TO THIS POLICY</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be communicated via email or a prominent notice on our website. The "Last reviewed" date at the top indicates the latest revision.</p>

    <h2 id="contact">16. CONTACT US</h2>
